1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,125
Where the hell're you goin'?!
C'mere, you damn mutt!

2
00:00:16,166 --> 00:00:18,166
Wait, you damn mutt!

3
00:00:18,166 --> 00:00:21,041
Don't run off with my EXP!

4
00:00:23,208 --> 00:00:25,125
Draconic Buster.

5
00:00:33,083 --> 00:00:36,000
That puts me at level 18.

6
00:00:47,166 --> 00:00:49,041
I... I can't.

7
00:00:49,041 --> 00:00:50,125
I can't do this after all.

8
00:00:50,125 --> 00:00:52,083
Kobato!

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,208
What are you doing spacing out?

10
00:00:54,208 --> 00:00:56,000
You'll get killed.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,125
Oh, Ikusaba-san...

12
00:00:57,208 --> 00:00:59,041
It's Asagi.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
I'm always saying how much I hate
being called by my family name.

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,125
If you're doing it on purpose,

15
00:01:05,125 --> 00:01:08,125
then 70 percent of the girls
in class will ostracize you.

16
00:01:08,125 --> 00:01:10,125
I-I'm sorry.

17
00:01:10,125 --> 00:01:12,000
Yeah, I forgive you!

18
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Listen, there's something I wanna
confirm with our harmless little pigeon.

19
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,208
What? Oh, um, sure.

20
00:01:17,208 --> 00:01:21,208
If I'm reading things right,
our class is probably gonna fall apart.

21
00:01:22,041 --> 00:01:23,000
Huh?

22
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,125
I mean, it's full of big egos,
you know what I'm saying?

23
00:01:26,125 --> 00:01:28,125
A lot of them are a pain, too.

24
00:01:28,125 --> 00:01:32,125
And to make matters worse, we've been
assigned ranks like S-Class and E-Class.

25
00:01:32,125 --> 00:01:34,166
Oh, by the way, I'm a B-Class.

26
00:01:35,041 --> 00:01:39,166
In due time, distinct factions
are going to splinter off for sure.

27
00:01:39,166 --> 00:01:42,000
When that happens...

28
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,166
of course you'll be joining mine, right?

29
00:01:45,166 --> 00:01:47,041
Won't you?

30
00:01:47,166 --> 00:01:51,166
As a D-Class, you won't make
it into Kirihara's group.

31
00:01:51,166 --> 00:01:54,041
And the Takao sisters are always a pair.

32
00:01:54,041 --> 00:01:56,208
Ayaka... is just going to die anyway, y'know?

33
00:01:56,208 --> 00:01:59,041
What? Sogou-san will?

34
00:01:59,041 --> 00:02:01,083
Wh-What do you mean by that?

35
00:02:01,083 --> 00:02:03,083
You don't get it, huh?

36
00:02:03,166 --> 00:02:04,208
At any rate,

37
00:02:04,208 --> 00:02:08,125
Kobato-chan, you should think long
and hard about where you stand.

38
00:02:08,208 --> 00:02:10,125
Depending on how things play out,

39
00:02:10,125 --> 00:02:14,208
if we manage to defeat this
Great Demon Empire and return to our world,

40
00:02:14,208 --> 00:02:18,125
then what we achieve here
could affect us back home,

41
00:02:18,125 --> 00:02:22,125
and you might find yourself
with nowhere to fit in, Kashima Kobato-chan.

42
00:02:23,083 --> 00:02:25,000
Even if your abilities suck,

43
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,166
I can always make good use
of these in a pinch, after all.

44
00:02:28,166 --> 00:02:31,166
So let's do our best together, little pigeon.

45
00:02:31,166 --> 00:02:32,208
Now with that...

46
00:02:33,166 --> 00:02:36,041
Bring it out, girls!

47
00:02:39,083 --> 00:02:40,083
That's...

48
00:02:40,083 --> 00:02:47,083
Our sweet little pigeon hasn't yet cleared
the test the goddess assigned us, right?

49
00:02:48,083 --> 00:02:50,166
So we're gonna help you out.

50
00:02:51,166 --> 00:02:55,083
The Asagi group is all going
to get stronger together.

51
00:02:55,083 --> 00:02:56,208
So hurry up and kill it.

52
00:02:56,208 --> 00:03:00,208
Or do you want to be
disposed of like Mimori?

53
00:03:03,041 --> 00:03:05,125
Hurry up!

54
00:03:16,125 --> 00:03:18,125
Good job, little pigeon!

55
00:03:18,125 --> 00:03:21,125
You've passed the test,
and that settles things!

56
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,083
Now you're one of us too, little pigeon.

57
00:03:41,083 --> 00:03:42,208
Mimori-kun...

58
00:03:47,208 --> 00:03:49,083
Don't worry.

59
00:03:49,083 --> 00:03:50,166
I won't abandon you.

60
00:03:57,208 --> 00:04:01,125
I'm sorry. I couldn't do anything.

61
00:04:13,125 --> 00:04:15,000
I...

62
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Mimori-kun!

63
00:05:55,125 --> 00:05:58,208
ENCOUNTER ~AVENGER(S)~
- Pity what happened with Sir Tooka Mimori.

64
00:05:58,208 --> 00:06:01,041
ENCOUNTER ~AVENGER(S)~
- I'm so sorry,

65
00:06:01,041 --> 00:06:05,041
but that ritual is a firm policy
of the Kingdom of Alion.

66
00:06:05,125 --> 00:06:09,083
You have my deepest apologies, Miss Sogou.

67
00:06:09,083 --> 00:06:10,041
No way...

68
00:06:10,125 --> 00:06:13,041
However, you don't have
time to wallow in sadness.

69
00:06:13,041 --> 00:06:15,041
The ritual is still ongoing.

70
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:19,000
These past few days,
while you've been sleeping away,

71
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:23,041
everyone else departed on a test
to determine if they can kill a monster.

72
00:06:23,041 --> 00:06:28,208
However, several have failed to take up arms
against the monsters and been disqualified.

73
00:06:29,041 --> 00:06:34,083
And we must ask that those who cannot
fulfill their duty as heroes take their leave.

74
00:06:34,083 --> 00:06:36,166
You mean to cull the weak?

75
00:06:36,166 --> 00:06:39,041
That is Alion's policy.

76
00:06:40,083 --> 00:06:42,041
Let me be clear, Goddess.

77
00:06:42,041 --> 00:06:43,166
Go right ahead.

78
00:06:43,166 --> 00:06:44,208
Please speak your mind.

79
00:06:45,083 --> 00:06:48,125
I do not agree with the
way you're doing things.

80
00:06:51,041 --> 00:06:55,000
Well, the world is full of all sorts
of people and opinions.

81
00:06:55,083 --> 00:06:58,166
As a goddess, I am tolerant of all.

82
00:06:58,166 --> 00:07:04,000
So I'm willing to brook
a slight difference of views.

83
00:07:04,208 --> 00:07:09,125
That said, we must dispose of the worthless.

84
00:07:09,125 --> 00:07:10,166
It's unfortunate.

85
00:07:10,166 --> 00:07:13,166
An S-Class hero is valuable to you, right?

86
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,041
Yes! Extraordinarily so.

87
00:07:17,041 --> 00:07:20,000
Then I'll do my duty as an S-Class hero

88
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,000
to make up for the students
who couldn't clear your test.

89
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:26,041
If I do that, will you call off
their disposal?

90
00:07:26,041 --> 00:07:29,208
My, how courageous!
What a wonderful proposal!

91
00:07:29,208 --> 00:07:32,041
I'd expect no less of an S-Class hero!

92
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:35,083
Now then, let us shake
hands in reconciliation.

93
00:07:35,083 --> 00:07:38,166
I do apologize for punching
you in the stomach,

94
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:44,083
even if it was to settle your hysterics
over the unusual nature of your situation.

95
00:07:49,041 --> 00:07:51,208
I have high hopes for you, Miss Sogou.

96
00:07:53,041 --> 00:07:54,041
Right.

97
00:07:58,083 --> 00:07:59,208
What cold hands...

98
00:08:00,208 --> 00:08:03,000
THE DARK FOREST

99
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:22,208
I thought I'd finally given them the slip!

100
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,041
"THE SWORD GOD" MAGATS BLAYDIN
- Still trying to run, huh?

101
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
You can conceal your presence,
but you suck at hiding, Princess Knight!

102
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,125
"THE OUTLANDISH DEMON" ASHURA
- You can conceal your presence,
but you suck at hiding, Princess Knight!

103
00:08:41,125 --> 00:08:43,125
"SUPER PRESSURE" JIOBANE SENGAI
- Should we reap her already?

104
00:08:43,125 --> 00:08:45,000
Don't be stupid!

105
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,083
The foreplay's just getting started!

106
00:08:47,083 --> 00:08:50,000
The least she can do is give us a little fun.

107
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,125
Right, Zarash?

108
00:08:52,083 --> 00:08:55,166
"THE FANG" ZARASH FINEBARD
- We'll have to start by carving
the truth into her soul.

109
00:08:56,041 --> 00:09:00,208
That any attempt at escape or resistance
is futile against us, the Holy Watchers.

110
00:09:00,208 --> 00:09:02,041
THE HOLY WATCHERS
- That any attempt at escape or resistance
is futile against us, the Holy Watchers.

111
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:03,041
THE HOLY WATCHERS

112
00:09:07,125 --> 00:09:09,000
Now then...

113
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,125
Stats: Open.

114
00:09:11,125 --> 00:09:12,166
TOOKA MIMORI
LV 1,789

115
00:09:12,166 --> 00:09:15,000
TOOKA MIMORI
LV 1,789
- Only my MP is exceptional.

116
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,166
TOOKA MIMORI
LV 1,789
- But what I want to confirm now is...

117
00:09:16,166 --> 00:09:17,125
But what I want to confirm now is...

118
00:09:17,125 --> 00:09:20,083
I can dismiss Paralyze at will.
On just the head, too.

119
00:09:20,083 --> 00:09:23,000
I can also dismiss Poison
or make it nonlethal.

120
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Guess I can avoid killing targets that way.

121
00:09:25,083 --> 00:09:27,166
Maybe I'll try it out if
there's a monster nearby.

122
00:09:30,208 --> 00:09:32,000
Next...

123
00:09:33,083 --> 00:09:34,125
I need a blade.

124
00:09:35,125 --> 00:09:36,125
A sword.

125
00:09:36,125 --> 00:09:39,125
Someone who can act as a tank
and handle the frontline for me.

126
00:09:45,083 --> 00:09:46,125
Are those...

127
00:09:47,166 --> 00:09:49,166
slimes?

128
00:09:59,208 --> 00:10:01,166
Don't let them get away with that.

129
00:10:08,166 --> 00:10:10,000
I guess that's that...

130
00:10:15,208 --> 00:10:17,000
That's the spirit!

131
00:10:19,041 --> 00:10:20,041
Paralyze.

132
00:10:21,041 --> 00:10:22,041
Poison.

133
00:10:22,125 --> 00:10:26,083
POISON (LETHAL)
- So I can change the setting from here, huh?

134
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:27,166
POISON (NONLETHAL)

135
00:10:27,166 --> 00:10:29,000
POISON (NONLETHAL)
- I see.

136
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,041
POISON (NONLETHAL)
- And this option dismisses it?

137
00:10:31,041 --> 00:10:35,041
PARALYZE (DISMISS)

138
00:10:35,041 --> 00:10:36,083
Get lost.

139
00:10:43,041 --> 00:10:45,083
I made it so you can't move,

140
00:10:45,083 --> 00:10:47,041
but I'm about to undo that.

141
00:10:47,041 --> 00:10:49,125
Don't worry.
I have no intention of killing you.

142
00:10:50,125 --> 00:10:53,000
Though I am going to say
something kinda haughty.

143
00:10:55,083 --> 00:10:57,166
Sorry for not helping you sooner.

144
00:10:58,083 --> 00:11:01,125
But, well, you did good.

145
00:11:01,125 --> 00:11:04,083
It was nice to see you stand
up for yourself against them.

146
00:11:05,083 --> 00:11:07,125
Don't attack me once you can move, okay?

147
00:11:07,125 --> 00:11:09,166
PARALYZE (DISMISS)

148
00:11:10,166 --> 00:11:12,000
Later.

149
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,083
Have a nice life.

150
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,166
Well, damn.

151
00:11:42,166 --> 00:11:44,166
You planning to keep following me?

152
00:11:48,125 --> 00:11:49,125
I see.

153
00:11:50,125 --> 00:11:53,083
You're an outcast just like me, aren't you?

154
00:11:57,041 --> 00:11:58,166
They're far away.

155
00:11:58,166 --> 00:12:01,083
But their presence still lingers.

156
00:12:01,083 --> 00:12:04,083
They're just waiting
for me to exhaust myself.

157
00:12:04,208 --> 00:12:08,208
So this is how the Holy Watchers
of heroic blood hunt...

158
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,125
Can you see behind me?

159
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Good. Now I have eyes in the back of my head.

160
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,041
Befriending you was the right move.

161
00:12:23,166 --> 00:12:24,166
Here we are.

162
00:12:24,166 --> 00:12:27,000
I see. A forbidden art, huh?

163
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,000
I guess it would be.

164
00:12:28,166 --> 00:12:30,166
An experiment to strengthen monsters...

165
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:34,000
It even describes how to craft
a solution to enhance slimes.

166
00:12:34,125 --> 00:12:37,125
Anglin was probably afraid
of this being misused.

167
00:12:38,125 --> 00:12:39,083
Hey.

168
00:12:40,125 --> 00:12:44,166
What I'm after is plain
old personal vengeance.

169
00:12:44,166 --> 00:12:47,166
I'm on a journey to that end.

170
00:12:48,041 --> 00:12:50,125
So you'll be going along with my ego.

171
00:12:50,125 --> 00:12:51,166
Are you okay with that?

172
00:12:52,208 --> 00:12:54,125
If you want out, now's your chance.

173
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Hmph, I see.

174
00:12:58,166 --> 00:13:02,166
Then I'll be counting on you, Piggymaru.

175
00:13:04,125 --> 00:13:06,083
That's your name.

176
00:13:06,083 --> 00:13:09,083
But if you have any objections,
I'm listening.

177
00:13:09,083 --> 00:13:11,041
PIGGYMARU
SLIME

178
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,083
Forbidden magic and arts...

179
00:13:15,083 --> 00:13:18,208
I'll use anything I can
to crush that goddess.

180
00:13:19,208 --> 00:13:22,083
I will get my revenge.

181
00:13:31,083 --> 00:13:32,208
They've closed the distance.

182
00:13:32,208 --> 00:13:34,041
I really can't shake them!

183
00:13:37,166 --> 00:13:39,125
I guess I'll have to use it.

184
00:13:40,166 --> 00:13:43,000
What I seek is the regalia of spirits.

185
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
By our pact,

186
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,125
I offer thee my sleep as payment...

187
00:13:51,125 --> 00:13:52,166
Silfigzea,

188
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Ferillbanger,

189
00:13:59,083 --> 00:14:00,125
Willozega!

190
00:14:09,083 --> 00:14:10,208
Spirit Regalia!

191
00:14:14,041 --> 00:14:15,083
Hmm?

192
00:14:15,083 --> 00:14:17,166
Who's this? He sure ain't the girl.

193
00:14:18,041 --> 00:14:19,166
Wh-Who are you?

194
00:14:20,208 --> 00:14:22,125
Some mangy brat?

195
00:14:22,125 --> 00:14:24,125
The mere sight of you disgusts me.

196
00:14:25,125 --> 00:14:29,041
Well, for now, go ahead
and drop all your valuables.

197
00:14:29,041 --> 00:14:31,041
Then we'll spare your life.

198
00:14:31,041 --> 00:14:33,208
No, we're killing him.

199
00:14:33,208 --> 00:14:38,041
I haven't tested this baby's edge
on a living human yet.

200
00:14:38,041 --> 00:14:41,125
So I'll try it out on this sack of trash.

201
00:14:41,125 --> 00:14:43,208
If you are, then make it quick, Magats.

202
00:14:44,083 --> 00:14:47,041
The girl should be running
out of stamina soon.

203
00:14:47,041 --> 00:14:51,166
The nice thing about men is there's
no wasting time enjoying them first!

204
00:14:51,166 --> 00:14:54,166
Not much fun in abusing 'em
before we kill 'em.

205
00:14:54,166 --> 00:14:57,041
Let's hurry up and catch the woman so we
can use the money at Ablom's brothel.

206
00:14:57,041 --> 00:15:01,041
Better yet, let's grab a good-looking
girl from a nearby town

207
00:15:01,041 --> 00:15:04,041
and drag her around for half a year
while we have fun breaking her.

208
00:15:04,041 --> 00:15:05,041
Screw you!

209
00:15:05,041 --> 00:15:09,166
No woman's ever lasted half a year
when you set out to break her!

210
00:15:09,166 --> 00:15:11,000
Shut up!

211
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,041
It's their fault for losing it so fast.

212
00:15:13,041 --> 00:15:16,208
Honestly, having our way with
that woman would be the best course.

213
00:15:16,208 --> 00:15:24,208
Man, I won't be satisfied with human
women after laying eyes on that bitch!

214
00:15:25,041 --> 00:15:30,208
Even so, we have to refrain from taking
advantage of our prey this time.

215
00:15:30,208 --> 00:15:33,083
Remember who paid for this job.

216
00:15:33,083 --> 00:15:38,125
So, where do you think you're going,
trying to back away in fright?

217
00:15:39,083 --> 00:15:40,125
Please...

218
00:15:40,125 --> 00:15:41,166
P-Please just let me go!

219
00:15:41,166 --> 00:15:44,041
I don't want to die here for nothing!

220
00:15:45,041 --> 00:15:47,083
I told you you're out of luck.

221
00:15:47,083 --> 00:15:53,000
I'll test this out on you quick,
then we have to get back to work.

222
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:58,083
- So go right the hell ahead
and fall victim to me, Magats!
- Paralyze.

223
00:15:58,083 --> 00:15:59,208
Whaâ€”

224
00:16:00,166 --> 00:16:01,208
Good.

225
00:16:01,208 --> 00:16:04,208
My status ailment skill
is effective on humans, too.

226
00:16:04,208 --> 00:16:07,083
I guess that damn goddess
is the only exception.

227
00:16:08,083 --> 00:16:09,083
Impossible!

228
00:16:09,083 --> 00:16:12,041
You're not as intimidating
as the monsters in the ruins.

229
00:16:12,041 --> 00:16:16,041
Though I guess your malice is
equal to or worse than theirs.

230
00:16:16,041 --> 00:16:19,166
I'm saying you're all scumbags.

231
00:16:20,125 --> 00:16:22,041
You're mad too?

232
00:16:22,208 --> 00:16:27,083
Of course. Well, it's not going to bother me
if these guys die.

233
00:16:27,083 --> 00:16:29,041
In fact, I think I'll feel better.

234
00:16:29,041 --> 00:16:31,000
Meet bloodlust with bloodlust.

235
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,166
Meet hostility with the same.

236
00:16:33,083 --> 00:16:35,125
In short, it means I can kill.

237
00:16:37,041 --> 00:16:39,000
Even facing humans, I can kill.

238
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:42,125
Poison.

239
00:16:48,083 --> 00:16:50,083
You can feel it too?

240
00:16:50,083 --> 00:16:51,208
Yeah, I know.

241
00:16:53,125 --> 00:16:55,208
There's someone else nearby.

242
00:16:57,041 --> 00:16:58,166
Their presence is gone?

243
00:16:59,208 --> 00:17:00,208
They're not moving?

244
00:17:02,166 --> 00:17:04,125
Are they plotting something?

245
00:17:08,125 --> 00:17:11,000
No, I can sense someone.

246
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,208
What is this feeling?

247
00:17:16,166 --> 00:17:20,000
Their presence isn't terribly strong,
but it's unsettling.

248
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,041
The spirits are frightened of it.

249
00:17:25,125 --> 00:17:26,166
Paralyze.

250
00:17:28,083 --> 00:17:30,166
I sensed your intent to attack,

251
00:17:30,166 --> 00:17:34,000
but there's something else
mixed in with your hostility.

252
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
It got me curious.

253
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:39,083
So I thought we could chat for a bit,

254
00:17:39,083 --> 00:17:42,083
though I'm keeping you
immobile as a precaution.

255
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:46,083
What... are you after?

256
00:17:46,166 --> 00:17:49,041
Well, I seem to be lost.

257
00:17:49,041 --> 00:17:51,166
I'm not from around here,

258
00:17:51,166 --> 00:17:54,000
so I'm not familiar these parts.

259
00:17:54,125 --> 00:17:58,000
I was hoping you could help fill me in.

260
00:17:58,083 --> 00:17:59,166
And the other four...?

261
00:17:59,166 --> 00:18:01,208
Are they friends of yours?

262
00:18:02,125 --> 00:18:04,041
Not at all...

263
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:06,208
I'm going to let you move your mouth now.

264
00:18:06,208 --> 00:18:10,125
If you try anything funny,
I'll use my skill again.

265
00:18:10,125 --> 00:18:12,083
PARALYZE (DISMISS)
- I'm bluffing.
- I have means of hurting you, too. Got it?

266
00:18:12,083 --> 00:18:14,083
PARALYZE (PARTIAL DISMISSAL: HEAD)
- It's impossible to stack Paralyze.
- I have means of hurting you, too. Got it?

267
00:18:14,083 --> 00:18:16,125
PARALYZE (PARTIAL DISMISSAL: HEAD)
- Though I didn't exactly lie.

268
00:18:16,125 --> 00:18:18,000
PARALYZE (PARTIAL DISMISSAL: HEAD)
- Understand?

269
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,083
PARALYZE (PARTIAL DISMISSAL: HEAD)
- Yes...

270
00:18:20,166 --> 00:18:23,166
I-I can speak normally now?

271
00:18:24,166 --> 00:18:26,208
Your mouth is all you can move.

272
00:18:26,208 --> 00:18:30,041
Sorry, but I'm still wary of you.

273
00:18:30,041 --> 00:18:32,208
I went through a lot on my way here,

274
00:18:32,208 --> 00:18:35,166
so I don't readily trust strangers.

275
00:18:36,041 --> 00:18:40,000
There is something I wish to confirm
before I answer your questions.

276
00:18:40,125 --> 00:18:42,208
Did you encounter a group of four?

277
00:18:42,208 --> 00:18:44,041
I did.

278
00:18:44,041 --> 00:18:45,083
Where are they now?

279
00:18:45,083 --> 00:18:46,125
I killed them.

280
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:49,208
What? You killed them?

281
00:18:49,208 --> 00:18:51,125
Is that a problem?

282
00:18:51,125 --> 00:18:54,083
No, but you slew the Holy Watchers...

283
00:18:54,083 --> 00:18:56,041
Don't tell me you did it all by yourself.

284
00:18:56,041 --> 00:18:58,208
Or do you have other allies nearby?

285
00:18:58,208 --> 00:19:00,000
Just one.

286
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,083
Though I don't intend
to reveal them at the moment.

287
00:19:03,083 --> 00:19:07,000
Thank you for humoring me.

288
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:11,166
I sensed no falsehood when you
claimed to have defeated those four.

289
00:19:11,166 --> 00:19:16,000
- I know you have answered me faithfully.
- She seems extremely confident
in her ability to discern lies.

290
00:19:16,125 --> 00:19:19,125
I will also answer your questions
as honestly as I can.

291
00:19:19,208 --> 00:19:22,125
You are my savior after a fashion, after all.

292
00:19:22,125 --> 00:19:25,083
You don't seem like a bad person to me.

293
00:19:25,083 --> 00:19:26,125
So far.

294
00:19:27,041 --> 00:19:30,000
Does that mean I've earned some of your trust?

295
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,125
A little.

296
00:19:31,125 --> 00:19:34,166
But like you, there are things
I'd rather not talk about.

297
00:19:34,166 --> 00:19:37,208
So I think it's best if neither of us
pries too much.

298
00:19:38,041 --> 00:19:40,166
Yes, I would be grateful for that.

299
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,208
Okay, then it's my turn to ask questions.

300
00:19:44,166 --> 00:19:46,041
I see...

301
00:19:46,041 --> 00:19:47,166
So this isn't Alion.

302
00:19:47,166 --> 00:19:49,208
It's a forest in the south
of the Kingdom of Ulza.

303
00:19:49,208 --> 00:19:52,208
I just assumed the Ruins of Disposal
were in Alion.

304
00:19:53,083 --> 00:19:54,208
One last question.

305
00:19:55,166 --> 00:19:57,166
Do you know anything about this writing?

306
00:19:58,125 --> 00:20:01,125
This... I believe it's ancient script.

307
00:20:01,125 --> 00:20:03,166
A rather unique variation, too.

308
00:20:03,166 --> 00:20:04,166
Can you read it?

309
00:20:05,125 --> 00:20:08,000
No, I'm afraid I cannot.

310
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
I see. Okay.

311
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,208
I'll just have to research it the hard way.

312
00:20:11,208 --> 00:20:16,166
However, I might know someone who
should be familiar with that writing.

313
00:20:17,083 --> 00:20:20,125
She was once known as the Witch of Taboos.

314
00:20:20,208 --> 00:20:24,208
She possessed such vast knowledge
of the forbidden in this world that

315
00:20:24,208 --> 00:20:26,000
she was deemed dangerous.

316
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,125
I heard she was driven
from her homeland.

317
00:20:28,125 --> 00:20:31,000
If I wanted to find her, where should I go?

318
00:20:31,083 --> 00:20:33,000
The Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters.

319
00:20:33,083 --> 00:20:35,083
Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters?

320
00:20:36,041 --> 00:20:39,083
It's a treacherous heartland of the continent.

321
00:20:39,083 --> 00:20:41,041
Thank you for the valuable tip.

322
00:20:41,125 --> 00:20:45,041
I cannot say I've repaid my debts.

323
00:20:45,041 --> 00:20:48,000
After all, you saved my life.

324
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,041
No, you can say we're even.

325
00:20:51,166 --> 00:20:53,208
So now we'll be parting ways.

326
00:20:53,208 --> 00:20:55,041
That's fine by you, right?

327
00:20:55,041 --> 00:20:56,125
Y-Yes.

328
00:20:56,125 --> 00:20:58,083
As long as you're satisfied.

329
00:20:58,083 --> 00:21:00,000
She's got a real sense of honor.

330
00:21:00,041 --> 00:21:02,125
For better or worse, she's too honest.

331
00:21:02,125 --> 00:21:04,041
She reminds me of my aunt.

332
00:21:04,041 --> 00:21:07,000
She was so nice that it
made me worry about her.

333
00:21:07,083 --> 00:21:09,083
I-Is something the matter?

334
00:21:09,083 --> 00:21:12,125
No. You'll be free in a few minutes,

335
00:21:12,125 --> 00:21:14,166
but I can't guarantee your
safety until then.

336
00:21:14,166 --> 00:21:15,208
I understand.

337
00:21:15,208 --> 00:21:18,083
I'll be released soon enough.

338
00:21:18,166 --> 00:21:24,166
Yeah. This may not mean much
after I ambushed you,

339
00:21:24,166 --> 00:21:27,083
but I'll pray for your safe travels.

340
00:21:40,166 --> 00:21:45,166
Yeah. It's not like I take
any delight in slaughter.

341
00:21:46,041 --> 00:21:48,041
I won't resort to pointless murder.

342
00:21:48,166 --> 00:21:51,125
I only kill in accordance with my own rules.

343
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:56,083
I can't deny the possibility
that woman will come after me

344
00:21:56,083 --> 00:21:59,000
to attack me once she's free to move.

345
00:21:59,125 --> 00:22:01,208
So keep watching my back.

346
00:22:02,083 --> 00:22:04,125
I'm counting on you, partner.

347
00:23:47,041 --> 00:23:49,083
That's a helluva bounty, ain't it?

348
00:23:49,083 --> 00:23:52,125
They say she was a paladin of Neah,
which got wiped out by Bakoss,

349
00:23:52,125 --> 00:23:55,208
and that she's the princess of that old
half-elf nation too, you know.

350
00:23:56,125 --> 00:24:00,000
If some ruffians captured
her for the bounty,

351
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:03,041
you think they'd hand over such
a beauty without having a taste?

352
00:24:03,041 --> 00:24:06,041
Anyone would want to try
fooling around with her.

353
00:24:06,166 --> 00:24:08,125
That Seras Ashrain.

354
00:24:10,166 --> 00:24:14,208
THE WOMAN KNOWN AS THE PRINCESS KNIGHT

